Package: universal-db-mcp
Version: 0.1.0
Section: database
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12~), python3-venv, libc6 (>= 2.36)
Recommends: systemd
Maintainer: Universal DB MCP Release Engineering <release-eng@example.invalid>
Description: Air-gapped MCP server for universal database access
 Universal DB MCP exposes PostgreSQL, MySQL/MariaDB, ClickHouse, Oracle,
 Microsoft SQL Server and Db2 to MCP clients behind a single hardened
 protocol. This package carries the signed offline bundle (installed under
 /usr/share/universal-db-mcp/bundle/) plus inert reference copies of the
 verification tools (/usr/share/universal-db-mcp/trusted-tools/), which the
 package never executes: the trusted verifier and installer live in the
 administrator-installed /usr/local/lib/udbmcp-trust directory.
 .
 Verify-before-execute: no payload code runs until postinst has re-verified
 the unpacked bundle with the trusted verify_bundle.py against the release
 public key that the administrator distributes out-of-band. The public key
 is never shipped inside this package, and any verification failure aborts
 the install before a single byte of the payload is executed (fail closed).
 .
 The Python virtual environment is built strictly offline with pip
 --no-index --require-hashes against the bundle's wheelhouse and
 runtime.lock, with pip configuration from the environment neutralized
 (PIP_CONFIG_FILE).
 .
 /etc/universal-db-mcp/config.yaml ships as a dpkg conffile: dpkg places it
 at unpack time (owner root:root, mode 0644), preserves admin edits across
 upgrades (prompting only on conflicts), retains it on package removal and
 deletes it on purge. The postinst additionally seeds it only if absent
 (owner udbmcp:udbmcp, mode 0640) from the verified bundle's
 config-templates/ copy, restoring a config an admin deleted before an
 upgrade; it never overwrites an existing file.
